Format the following UN resolution operative clauses. The parser detects structure from the numbering pattern, not indentation.

Numbering hierarchy:
- Main clauses: 1., 2., 3. (Arabic numerals with period)
- First-level sub-clauses: I., II., III. (Roman numerals with period)
- Second-level sub-clauses: a), b), c) (lowercase letters with parenthesis)
- Third-level sub-clauses: aa), bb), cc) (double letters with parenthesis)

End each clause with a semicolon (;), final clause with a period (.).

Example format:
1. Calls upon all Member States to;
I. develop national action plans;
II. strengthen international cooperation;
a) through bilateral agreements;
b) through multilateral frameworks;
2. Requests the Secretary-General to submit a report.

